<!-- markdownlint-disable MD024 -->
# parallel-agent-swarm-dispatch-patterns — History

## v1.4.0 (2026-05-31)

**Changed by:** ProjectHephaestus 10-PR audit-remediation swarm session (2026-05-31) — same
session that drove v1.3.0, but drilling into the prompt-engineering recipe for the residual
case where Part 12's sequential-single-agent bundling is impossible (DAG, external-event
gate, or chain length exceeds a single agent's working budget).
**Verification:** verified-ci (v3 unified PR8+PR10 sequential agent ran end-to-end; PR8/#869
merged, PR10/#870 CI green with auto-merge armed). Stacks additively on the v1.3.0 Part 12
decision rule that landed in PR #2075.

### What changed

- Added **Part 13** — Dependency-Gate Loop Early-Exit Hardening (sub-agent SELF quits at loop
  start). Distinct from Part 12 (decision rule chain → 1 agent / fan-out → N agents) and from
  v1.2.0 Part 11 #5 (anti-early-exit for FOREGROUND test runs); Part 13 targets the specific
  failure mode where the SUB-AGENT itself self-terminates at the FIRST iteration of an
  `until <gh-issue closedAt>` dependency-gate polling loop, even when bundling is not feasible.
  Four discrete techniques: (1) never use a polling loop as the FIRST instruction — restructure
  as a hard-capped `for i in $(seq 1 N)` loop with explicit success branch + FATAL `exit 1` on
  cap; (2) IMMEDIATELY after the loop, include `**DO NOT STOP HERE. Proceed immediately to
  Step 1.**` on its own line so the directive survives the agent's internal summarization;
  (3) ABSOLUTE RULE block at the TOP of the prompt listing "waiting" / "monitor running" /
  "gate is polling" as explicit FAILURE states; (4) STRONGLY PREFER one SEQUENTIAL agent for
  both phases (matches Part 12 #4) — the "wait for my OWN just-pushed PR" loop does NOT trigger
  the early-exit reflex, only "wait for sibling agent's PR" does. Added a decision table for
  gate strategy (single PR, 2 PRs with dependency, 3+ linear chain, 3+ DAG, external event)
  that defers to Part 12 / Part 13 #4 wherever sequential-single-agent applies.
- Added an `### Quick Reference` "Dependency-gate sub-agent prompt template (Part 13)" and a
  companion "STRONGLY PREFER: sequential-single-agent template (Part 13 #4 / Part 12 #4)".
- Added 3 new Failed Attempts rows (40, 41, 42, continuing after Part 12's rows 38–39): bare
  `until` loop as first instruction (PR8 v1), prose-above-loop "DO NOT exit early" note
  (PR10 v1 + v2), and dispatching one gated agent per dependent PR (PR8 separate from PR10).
- Added a "Dependency-gate loop early-exit incidents (ProjectHephaestus, 2026-05-31)" table to
  Results & Parameters with the v1/v2/v3 attempts, plus a "Validation parameters for hard-capped
  gate loops" table (`MAX_CYCLES`, `sleep`, FATAL exit code, "DO NOT STOP HERE" placement).
- Added 7 new tags (deduped against v1.3.0's): `dependency-gate`, `polling-loop`, `until-loop`,
  `sequential-single-agent`, `hard-cap-iteration`, `do-not-stop-here`, `absolute-rule-block`.
  (`gate-loop` was already added in v1.3.0; not re-added.)
- Added description trigger (13) for the gate-loop hardening pattern.
- Added 2 new "When to Use" bullets: gate-loop hardening as the FIRST-instruction restructure
  rule; sequential-single-agent preference over multiple gated agents on shared
  merge-dependencies (cross-references Part 12 / Part 13 #4).
- Added a second ProjectHephaestus 2026-05-31 row to Verified On covering the Part 13 evidence
  (gate-loop early-exit hardening; complements the v1.3.0 row covering the Part 12 decision
  rule).
- Updated the Overview Outcome paragraph with the v1.4.0 summary; bumped version 1.3.0 → 1.4.0
  (date stays 2026-05-31 since both updates came from the same session).

### Why

v1.3.0's Part 12 established the decision rule: dependency chain → 1 sequential agent;
fan-out → N concurrent agents gated on the join point. That covers the case where the chain
can be collapsed into a single agent. But the same 2026-05-31 session also surfaced cases
where collapsing is NOT possible (DAG topology, external-event gates, chain too long for one
agent's working budget) — and the early-exit failure mode hits HARDER there because there is
no escape via bundling. THREE separate gated agents (PR8 v1, PR10 v1, PR10 v2) early-exited at
the first iteration of their `until` polling loops; the orchestrator burned ~3 hours and 3
agent invocations re-launching them.

Part 13 codifies the prompt-engineering recipe that prevents the early-exit reflex on the
gates that cannot be eliminated. The four techniques (hard-capped `for` loop, post-loop
`**DO NOT STOP HERE**` directive, top-of-prompt ABSOLUTE RULE block, and the
"prefer sequential-single-agent" guidance that cross-references Part 12 #4) are empirically
validated: applying them to the v3 unified PR8+PR10 agent collapsed 3 failed attempts into 1
successful run.

Part 12 (decision rule) and Part 13 (gate-hardening recipe) are complementary: Part 12 tells
you when you CAN avoid the gate (bundle into one agent), and Part 13 tells you how to harden
the gate when you CAN'T avoid it. Together they close the loop on dependency-gate failures
observed in the 2026-05-31 swarm.

This learning was also session-locally captured as the user-memory rule
`swarm-agents-quit-early-on-polling` but lacked the verified-ci v3 unified-agent solution and
the four-technique hardening recipe. v1.4.0 elevates it to a permanent Mnemosyne skill
amendment.

### Previous version (v1.3.0) snapshot

The v1.4.0 change is purely additive — Part 13, the dependency-gate prompt template, the
sequential-single-agent template, rows 40–42, the Part 13 evidence table, the validation-knobs
table, the new tags/triggers, and the second Verified On row were appended; no Part 1–12
content, no v1.3.0 Failed Attempts row, no v1.3.0 table was removed or rewritten. The v1.3.0
state (which itself preserves v1.2.0 → v1.1.0 → v1.0.0 additively) is recoverable as this file
MINUS the v1.4.0 additions listed above, and via git history of
`skills/parallel-agent-swarm-dispatch-patterns.md`.

