## v1.2.0 (2026-05-29)

**Changed by:** ProjectHephaestus audit-finding parallel remediation swarm session (2026-05-29)
**Verification:** verified-ci (4 PRs #688/#690/#691/#689 all merged green in CI; a 5th conditional PR queued)

### What changed

- Added **Part 11** — Audit-Finding Parallel Remediation Swarm (one PR per agent): the end-to-end
  recipe for turning a strict-audit finding list (~20 findings) into concurrent, conflict-free PRs.
  Eight numbered patterns: (1) thematic-PR batching with one `Closes #N` per PR, (2) orchestrator
  creates REAL issues FIRST and bakes each concrete number into the agent prompt (anti-fabrication),
  (3) pre-dispatch file-collision matrix, (4) isolated worktree per agent branched from fresh
  origin/main, (5) anti-early-exit prompting (FOREGROUND tests; not done until PR exists AND
  `autoMergeRequest` non-null), (6) dependent-PR sequencing, (7) full-auto autonomy + trust-but-verify,
  (8) per-worktree editable-install env quirk.
- Added an `### Quick Reference` "audit-finding parallel-remediation orchestrator checklist" plus a
  full-fix (`Closes #N`) variant of the dispatch-prompt template.
- Added 5 new "When to Use" bullets (parallel audit remediation, one-issue-per-PR reconciliation,
  anti-fabrication, file-collision matrix, dependent-PR sequencing).
- Added 7 new Failed Attempts rows (31–37): trimming a version matrix a consistency hook depends on,
  stale local `git ls-files` index vs `git ls-tree -r origin/main`, agents fabricating `Closes #N`,
  concurrent agents editing the same file, premature "tests probably fine" exit, missing editable
  install in a fresh worktree, and racing a dependent PR instead of sequencing it.
- Added 11 new tags: `audit-remediation`, `thematic-pr`, `one-issue-per-pr`, `issue-first`,
  `fabricated-issue-number`, `anti-early-exit`, `foreground-test`, `dependent-pr-sequencing`,
  `worktree-dev-install`, `stale-index`, `ci-matrix-consistency`.
- Added description triggers (9)–(11); added a ProjectHephaestus 2026-05-29 row to Verified On.
- Updated Overview Outcome paragraph with the v1.2.0 summary; bumped version 1.1.0 → 1.2.0,
  date 2026-05-28 → 2026-05-29.

### Why

The skill covered intra-repo swarm dispatch (file ownership, hot-file bundling, trust-but-verify,
pre-dispatch re-grade) but had no end-to-end recipe for the common case of remediating a large
audit-finding list with one background agent per thematic PR. The 2026-05-29 ProjectHephaestus
session ran this end-to-end and surfaced verified-ci patterns and failure modes not previously
captured: the one-`Closes #N`-per-PR reconciliation against a `pr-policy` gate, the issue-first
anti-fabrication discipline (agents invent fake issue numbers otherwise), the cross-PR
file-collision matrix (two PRs both wanted `loop_runner.py` and `auto-tag.yml`), anti-early-exit
prompting for background agents, dependent-PR sequencing, and the fresh-worktree editable-install
quirk. Two failed approaches are recorded as anti-patterns: dedup-by-trimming-a-version-matrix
broke a `check_python_version_consistency` hook, and verifying merged state via a stale local index
masked a merged deletion (use `git ls-tree -r origin/main`).

### Previous version (v1.1.0) snapshot

The v1.2.0 change is purely additive — Part 11, the Quick Reference checklist, rows 31–37, and the
new tags/triggers were appended; no prior Part 1–10 content, Failed Attempts row, or table was
removed or rewritten. The v1.1.0 state is therefore fully recoverable as this file MINUS the
additions listed above, and via git history of `skills/parallel-agent-swarm-dispatch-patterns.md`.
See the v1.1.0 entry below and the consolidated source snapshots further down for prior content.

